successfully converted into  other media formats in 1934  just a year after the first prairie  mason novel delighted readers the first  perry mason movie the case of the  howling dog was released within three  years time  warner brothers would release a total of  six perry mason movies  based on gardner's stories four of them  starring warren william as the world's  greatest attorney  how did you know i went there it's my  business to know things  give me the details the perry mason  radio program a 15-minute cereal that  ran  five afternoons a week from 1943 to 1955  on cbs radio  more closely resembled gardner's crime  and action filled novels  as opposed to the somber  courtroom-dominated tv series  the radio show was popular enough that  in 1956  cbs radio tried to move it format intact  to cbs television  but gardner said no leading the network  to adapt it into the long-running  daytime drama the edge of night  the original perry mason tv series ran  from 1957 to 1966  and as a full season of a show back then  ran around 30 episodes  a whopping 271 installments were  produced  that provided syndicators with a huge  volume of content to rerun on local  stations  hundreds of times over the ensuing 50  odd years perry mason wasn't a  serialized show  each episode generally focused on a  single case wrapped up within the  self-contained story so even dedicated  fans probably wouldn't notice that the  rerun package was one episode short for  years  the oliver twist inspired february 1966  installments the case of the twice told  twist is otherwise a run-of-the-mill  episode  except for the fact that it was produced  in full color the only episode in the  original series run not presented in  black and white  and now we see you for what you really  are as color took hold of tv by the mid  60s  twice told twist was a test to see how  mason would look if it were renewed for  a 10th season  but it wasn't meant to be star raymond  bird told the washington post in 1986  when we got to the end of nine  they asked me for one more year in color  and they shot one show in colour and i  said no  with no tenth season there were no more  color episodes of perry mason  at least not this version of the series  anyway  perry mason was so good at arguing his  case in front of a judging jury that  unlike a real life attorney his win-loss  ratio leaned staggeringly in favor of  the former  268 wins and three losses after all he  was a good guy in the title character  and in the relatively quaint world of  early television it would have been  unthinkable for him to actually lose a  case  in order to balance shocking twists with  his winning record show writers  sometimes used some courtroom  maneuvering  to give the lawyer technical victories  after the fact the 1963 episode the case  of the deadly verdict  begins with a confused mason receiving a  guilty verdict and a death sentence for  his client  accused of murder but then he  investigates and finds a real killer his  lust turns into another win  in 1958 the case of the terrified typist  mason's defendant is found guilty  but is later revealed to be a trickster  pretending to be the real bad guy  your honor this is just another  wild-eyed dramatic grandstand play for  which council is so noted  mason's only actual last came in 1963 as  a case of the witless witness  an episode that begins with the attorney  losing an appeal a rare but relatively  minor loss for the improbably capable  attorney  by the early 1970s the soldier for  decades very recently gone by was in  full swing  fans of 50s culture helped turn greece  into a broadway smash  and make american graffiti a blockbuster  movie on tv  show starring gold favorites and  revivals of classics filled network's  schedules  everything old was new again in 1973  alone  cbs programs the new bill cosby show the  new dick van dyke show and the new perry  mason the original perry mason show had  only been off the air for seven years at  that point and none of the original cast  returned for the reboot  instead of bringing back raymond burr  producers hired lesser known actor monty  marcum to take over for burr in the  iconic role of perry mason  cbs was apparently so confident in the  project that according to markham they  bypassed the pilot and ordered it  straight to series asking for 26  episodes  but only 15 installments aired before  cbs cancelled the new perry mason which  finished the season with low ratings in  1974.  out of 80 shows the new take on an old  favorite reportedly ranked in  at number 71. despite the failure of the  new perry mason on cbs the undefeatable  attorney returned to television a mere  11 years later  this time it was on nbc and in a  different format a succession of  semi-regular made for tv movies this  time bringing back the biggest names  from the original the ones who were  still alive at least  raymond burr returned as perry mason and  so did barbara hale at secretary della  street the role of investigator paul  drake played by the deceased william  hopper was reworked as paul drake jr  and hale's real-life son william katz  took the part perry mason showed up on  tv  three or four times a season for a  two-hour time slot in these formulaic  matlock-esque films  in which a crime was investigated and  then tried in intense courtroom scenes  a total of 26 perry mason movies aired  between 1985  and 1993. perry mason the case of the  killer kiss was the last project  bird would star in with a movie airing  two months after his death the made for  tv mason movies was so reliable for nbc  that the network kept the franchise  going for two years after burst passing  in four movies with the umbrella title  at perry mason mystery  the character perry mason is said to be  out of town and memorable lawyers  anthony caruso  played by paul savino and wild bill  mckenzie played by hal holbrook  argues some very very masonesque cases  in his absence  the perry mason character more or less  died when raymond byrd did in 1993  but in 2011 plans began in earnest to  revive the cracker jack attorney and his  cast of characters for a feature film  starring one of the biggest movie stars  in the world robert downey jr and his  wife producer susan downey  set the project up at warner brothers  with the iron man actor also serving as  the lead actor and co-writer  the script was to be based on a brand  new perry mason story  set in the dark and seedy los angeles of  gardner's novels but he wrote with  production associate david gambino  the movie never got off the ground but  in 2016 the project shifted to hbo where  execs were eager to make a new perry  mason  show and hired true detective creator  nick pizzalatto to write the episodes  a year later however pizzellato had  dropped out in favor of a third season  of true detective and hbo brought in  weeds and friday night lightswriters  roland jones and ron fitzgerald  the series was further delayed when  downey decided to serve only as an  executive producer on perry mason  and not acting it opening the door for  the emmy-winning star of the americans  matthew reese finally in march 2019  hbo officially ordered a mason mini  series  you've done such a great job on this  perry mason  series when matthew reese got the offer  to play perry mason he was initially  skeptical  he recalled in an interview with  collider i got this message saying they  want to talk to you about a remake of  perry mason  and i was like why would you want to  remake perry mason you can't remake  perry mason  i don't know if that's a good idea when  reese receives a full context of the  offer from his agent that it was an hbo  reimagining of perry mason  his interest peaked he said at the pitch  meeting with the producers and writers  i realized very quickly that it wasn't a  remake it's a firm reimagining and a  redefining of perry mason  in a very interesting way then when  production got moving along  reese realized his initial aversion to  stepping into the shoes of a classic  character  was even more misguided because upon  reflection he realized that he had few  concrete preconceived notions of the  show and his main character  he told npr i for one had this image of  who perry mason was and then you have  these vague memories of people  confessing on the stand  but i had no real specifics of perry  mason nevertheless rhys became  interested in the role  finding it to be quote a very dark perry  mason to which i was instantly attracted  he's also not nearly as experienced in  his role as an attorney providing an  opportunity to see the early days of a  fictional icon  much in the same way the movie casino  royale showed a version of secret agent  james bond before he was  you know james bond you may have heard  him i'm new to this  sustained see what i mean the perry  mason of hbo's 2020 reimagining is  nothing like the perry mason of days  past  not yet an established criminal defense  attorney the mason portrayed by matthew  reese is more like the one from  gardner's novels  a broke bitter private detective  complicated and burdened  still suffering from ptsd years after  fighting in world war one  haunted by a divorce and self-medicating  with alcohol  you're terrible are you drunk probably  jesus  perry despite putting all of its  significant resources into producing and  promoting its perry mason origin series  hbo apparently didn't have exceptionally  high expectations for how the series  would perform  according to entertainment weekly the  network initially billed the program as  a one-off mini-series  that way if it failed to attract viewers  over the course of its eight episodes  the network could limit the perception  of failure  but all of that trepidation was for  naught the series premiere episode in  june 2020  attracted 1.7 million viewers the cable  service's biggest debut in two years  out drawing recent hits like the  outsider and watchman within a month  perry mason had an audience of 8 million  leading hbo to reclassify the show  and then renew it for season 2. check  out one of our newest videos right here  plus even more looper videos about your  favorite movies and tv shows are coming  soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]  you

